WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:09.090
"The Wall Street journal" is now reporting
that Wagner chief yevgeny prigozhin had originally

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:15.080
intended to capture two of Putin's top military
leaders as part of his March on Moscow and

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:21.260
when intelligence agents discovered the plot
prigozhin was forced to move up his time line.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:26.939
Joining us with more on the real impact of
all of this, former CIA director and centcom

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:29.119
commander general David Petraeus.

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:30.920
Thank you for being here.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:38.770
If these details check out that prigozhin
planned to kidnap two military leaders as

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:44.510
part of his rebellion and also what "The new
York Times" is reporting that a top Russian

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:50.720
commander knew of prigozhin's plan ahead of
time, what then do you make of Putin allowing

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.700
yevgeny prigozhin to escape to exile in Belarus?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.700
[11:32:25 AM]

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.700
escape to exile in Belarus?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.699
Does it add up?

00:00:58.699 --> 00:01:05.150
&gt;&gt; Well, keep in mind that the Wagner group
is still a very useful tool in the foreign

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.850
policy arsenal of the Russian Federation.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:13.810
In fact, the foreign minister came out yesterday
and said it would still be active in Mali

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:19.049
and the central African republic and elsewhere
in the African republic and Syria and so forth.

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:24.890
It has been very helpful to the Russian cause
in those areas and they don't have a replacement

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:25.890
for that yet.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.100
It is also largely self-financing abroad.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.460
We know now that some of the financing for
the actions in Russia and Ukraine were coming

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:39.970
from the Russian Federation, but the whole
affair is just nothing short of fantastic.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:44.420
It reveals how desperate prigozhin had to
feel.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:49.600
His contracts were cut off and that his soldiers
would have to sign contracts with the ministry

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.220
of defense and he was going to lose his army
and his Russian source of revenue and he was

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.220
so

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.220
[11:33:26 AM]

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.939
source of revenue and he was so desperate
that he would launch this fantastical expedition

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:06.829
to kidnap the minister of defense and the
chief of the general staff whom he'd been

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:12.080
criticizing, of course, publicly for many
months and then right before that, of course,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.010
he also criticized the overall decision to
invade Ukraine and then the way in which the

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.450
war was being conducted.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.310
So really an extraordinary moment and then
Putin, of course, disappears and he was awol

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.489
in the day of this operation.

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:30.790
He took the ride, unlike president zelenskyy
at the start of the war, this last invasion

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.140
and he has to now reassert himself.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.510
He's got to show that he's still firmly in
charge.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:44.420
He does allow prigozhin again to go to president
lukashenko in Belarus where again you'll sort

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:49.739
out, but he has an investigation launch against
prigozhin perhaps as leverage if he needs

00:02:49.739 --> 00:02:54.130
it at some point in time and there is an extradition
treaty with Belarus.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.130
[11:34:27 AM]

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.130
Belarus.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:03:01.100
So again, we'll see how Putin is able to re-establish
himself now, but in the meantime, this weakens

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:05.790
the Russian forces on the battlefield at a
time when it appears that Ukraine is starting

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:10.560
to ground out some gains and still in the
early days and we still don't know where the

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.489
main effort is going to be.

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:18.590
I want to ask you on those fronts, the thing
that we haven't seen prigozhin in Belarus,

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:21.620
does that mean anything to you?

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:27.310
&gt;&gt; No, I think he's probably trying to figure
out what is his posture going to be going

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.310
forward?

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:33.390
Is he going to start criticizing the minister
of defense and the chief of the general staff.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.480
I suspect not for a while, at least.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:42.340
I think he realizes how close he came to again
ending up, you know, poked by an umbrella

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:48.500
or falling out of a window and he still needs
to be careful about both of those, so -- and

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:53.030
I'm sure that lukashenko has him a bit under
wraps as well and part of the deal was you

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:56.920
keep this guy quiet and keep him under control
and we'll sort out what

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.920
[11:35:28 AM]

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.720
control and we'll sort out what the future
is, keeping in mind again that the Wagner

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.159
group abroad is a useful tool for Russian
foreign policy.

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:07.480
&gt;&gt; I was just handed this because we have
new reporting coming in kind of getting to

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.420
what was going on behind the scenes, general,
I want to ask you about.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:17.560
A European intelligence says there were hints
that Russian security services might have

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:23.310
had notice of the rebellion this weekend and
key to this, of what we were talking about

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:27.000
off the top, might have wanted it to succeed.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:33.910
I'm kind of curious, when you hear that what
Putin should do now?

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:38.240
Does another military shake-up amongst the
ranks under Putin seem like that could be

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.710
in the offing right now?

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:47.139
&gt;&gt; Well, I don't think he wants to do this
immediately because it will do what prigozhin

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:51.220
had recommended be done which was to fire
the minister and fire the chief of the general

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.220
staff.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.820
So I don't think he wants to do this in the
short term because it would seem to respond

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.540
to what prigozhin was -- was counseling,

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.540
[11:36:30 AM]

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.930
prigozhin was -- was counseling, but look,
no.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:00.930
He's a student history.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:04.919
He knows that history is unkind to Russian
leaders who lose wars.

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:10.590
He's got to try to figure out how to stabilize
the front lines in the face of this mounting

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:17.000
summer offensive by the Ukrainian forces that
have additional training and all kinds of

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.720
other combat support and service support elements.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:24.669
So that's really got to be his focus.

00:05:24.669 --> 00:05:30.780
How does he avoid losing this war noting that
the leaders who lost the ruso-japanese war

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.639
in World War I did not stick around after
that.

00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:40.720
There may be people around the security services
and intelligence services who are starting

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.669
to think, you know, maybe we should consider
what might come after Putin.

00:05:44.669 --> 00:05:48.460
&gt;&gt; Something, a thought that -- he's been,
what?

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.860
His grip on power has been 23 years.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:56.880
A thought that probably has not crossed the
minds of many amongst his ranks for a very

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.680
long time if at all.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.710
You were in Ukraine last month

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:01.710
[11:37:30 AM]

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.430
You were in Ukraine last month and there's
been a lot said about the counteroffensive

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.380
under way in Ukraine so far.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:12.090
Do you have con fidence in the Ukrainian counteroffensive?

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:19.500
&gt;&gt; I am cautiously optimistic that the Ukrainian
forces are going to do what no force on either

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:23.000
side has done so far which is to put it all
together.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:31.960
Tanks, infantry, artillery, engineers, air
defense, drones, good command and control

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:37.320
and follow-on forces right up behind the lead
elements so that when they culminate after

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:42.900
72 or 96 hours as is typically the case in
tough fighting, you can maintain the momentum

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.460
and they can crack the Russian lines.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:50.630
We just don't know where that will be and
I'm not sure the Ukrainians do because in

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:56.090
probing attacks and reconnaissance in force
across the 600-mile front.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:58.840
Think of the distances here and how tough
it is to put forces in

00:06:58.840 --> 00:06:59.840
[11:38:31 AM]

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:04.980
how tough it is to put forces in position,
set the conditions as they say for the main

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.940
effort to be launched, and so it's hard to
say when that will come.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.259
We know it's very tough.

00:07:10.259 --> 00:07:16.870
Again, multiple belts of minefields, obstacles,
trenches, defense in depth and so forth, and

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:25.060
the Russians are doing this phase fairly competently,
but I do think at some point in time the Ukrainians

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:30.539
will break through and hopefully the morale
of the Russians has been damaged a bit by

00:07:30.539 --> 00:07:35.770
this whole episode, as well because prigozhin
has said what a lot of people are thinking

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.819
that this is not going well.

00:07:37.819 --> 00:07:43.280
It was probably a mistake and you know, who
wants to be the one that's the last to die

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:45.960
for this war that is not going well?

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.990
The Ukrainians know what they're fighting
for.

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:53.249
This is their war of Independence and the
Russians are much less certain about that.

00:07:53.249 --> 00:08:01.809
&gt;&gt; General David Petraeus, it is

